---
args: {"journal": "WarehouseJournal", "receipt": "InventoryReceipt"}
returns: "InventoryReceiptReview"
---
1. Find the pending work or adjustment by receipt.operationId and its expected ledger version in journal. Bind findings = checkCustodyConservation(journal, receipt). Missing operation identity, incomplete movement/adjustment evidence, a conflicting prior receipt, or stale bin version leaves bins unchanged. Return InventoryReceiptReview { journal: the unchanged journal with only the affected existing adjustment marked unknown when an actual ambiguous outcome is established, reconciledOperationIds: [], residualDifferences: the exact binding and conservation findings }.
2. For an already applied operation with identical movementReceiptId, adjustmentReceiptId, returned bin versions and quantities, return { journal, reconciledOperationIds: [receipt.operationId], residualDifferences: [] } without changing any quantity or revision. Conflicting reused receipt identity remains unresolved; never apply its delta twice.
3. When every required binding and conservation check passes, bind updatedBins to the exact receipt.binsAfter for the affected item/lot/location partitions, preserving all unrelated bins and actual custody records. Bind updatedAdjustments to the matching adjustment with its authoritative movement and adjustment receipt IDs and state applied; a pure movement needs the specific movement receipt required by its work kind.
4. Bind nextJournal as WarehouseJournal { revision: journal.revision + 1, cursors: journal.cursors, observations: journal.observations, identities: journal.identities, bins: updatedBins, work: journal.work with only evidenced completed work retired from its pending view, adjustments: updatedAdjustments, consumedEventIds: journal.consumedEventIds }. Return { journal: nextJournal, reconciledOperationIds: [receipt.operationId], residualDifferences: remaining differences not settled by this receipt }. Physical presence, available quantity and customer fulfillment remain separate facts.
